<title>UK: HORSE RACING-QUEEN ELIZABETH II STAKES RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-QUEEN ELIZABETH II STAKES RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>ASCOT, England 1996-09-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group one</p>
<p>Queen Elizabeth II Stakes for three-year-olds and upwards, run</p>
<p>over one mile (1.6 kms) on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Mark of Esteem 100-30 (Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>2. Bosra Sham 100-30 (Pat Eddery)</p>
<p>3. First Island 11-2 (Michael Hills)</p>
<p>Seven ran. Ashkalani 9-4 favourite</p>
<p>Distances: One and a quarter lengths, four</p>
<p>Winner owned by Godolphin Racing and trained by Saeed Bin</p>
<p>Suroor.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 199,020 sterling ($310,700)</p>
</text>
